{"id":"effect-ea9a381c-497b-5d6b-ae62-69ab739af111","sessionId":"0e254593-63da-5b08-edd4-0783fc8f47be","turnId":"turn-2fbe37e107ed938e2b9446d95c487b5d","inputEntryId":"user-turn-2fbe37e107ed938e2b9446d95c487b5d-1","createdAt":1794276857189,"updatedAt":1794276857216,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.read_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.read_file","display":{"summary":"Reading README.md","content":null,"suffix":"","verb":"Reading","message":"README.md","settledVerb":"Read","settledMessage":"README.md","statusText":"Reading file"},"kind":"file_read","input":{"filePath":"README.md","offset":null,"limit":2000}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","durationMs":0.0,"output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-RJbWKp/README.md","content":"# stories-api\n\nA small story library behind `POST /stories` (Lambda + DynamoDB table `stories`,\npartition key `slug`). `src/app.py` is the whole service: `handler()` parses\nthe request and `publish()` stores the story together with its three most\nsimilar existing stories (`similar: [{slug, score}]`), so the reader page can\nshow \"related\" without any query at read time. `logs/error.log` is the\nproduction log from the first two publishes after the deploy.\n\nTests use an in-memory table (`tests/fake_dynamo.py`) that validates items the\nway boto3 does, so no AWS account is needed. Run them with\n`python3 -m unittest discover tests` from the repo root.\n","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"requestedOffset":null,"requestedLimit":2000,"totalLines":null,"wasTruncated":false},"decision":"execute","approvalSource":"bypass","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Read","message":"12 lines from README.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"approvalType":"always"}}
