{"id":"effect-3d998f10-d6d8-5831-8050-13b9ae0a5175","sessionId":"0e254593-63da-5b08-edd4-0783fc8f47be","turnId":"turn-2fbe37e107ed938e2b9446d95c487b5d","inputEntryId":"user-turn-2fbe37e107ed938e2b9446d95c487b5d-1","createdAt":1794276887597,"updatedAt":1794276887605,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"vibe.todo","detail":{"toolName":"vibe.todo","display":{"summary":"Writing 4 todos","content":null,"suffix":"","verb":"Updating","message":"4 todos","settledVerb":"Updated","settledMessage":"4 todos","statusText":"Managing todos"},"kind":"todo","input":{"action":"write","todos":[{"id":"1","content":"Analyze error log and identify root cause","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"2","content":"Fix the float type issue in similarity/related functions","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"3","content":"Run tests to verify the fix","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"4","content":"Create ANSWER.md with cause and fix","status":"in_progress","priority":"medium"}]}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"{\"verb\": \"Updated\", \"todos\": [{\"id\": \"1\", \"content\": \"Analyze error log and identify root cause\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"priority\": \"medium\"}, {\"id\": \"2\", \"content\": \"Fix the float type issue in similarity/related functions\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"priority\": \"medium\"}, {\"id\": \"3\", \"content\": \"Run tests to verify the fix\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"priority\": \"medium\"}, {\"id\": \"4\", \"content\": \"Create ANSWER.md with cause and fix\", \"status\": \"in_progress\", \"priority\": \"medium\"}], \"total_count\": 4, \"message\": \"Updated 4 todos\"}","durationMs":0.0,"output":{"todos":[{"id":"1","content":"Analyze error log and identify root cause","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"2","content":"Fix the float type issue in similarity/related functions","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"3","content":"Run tests to verify the fix","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"4","content":"Create ANSWER.md with cause and fix","status":"in_progress","priority":"medium"}]},"decision":"execute","approvalSource":"bypass","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Updated","message":"4 todos","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"approvalType":"always"}}
{"id":"effect-a8d947c5-ba3f-50fc-af74-fbe4fb3f6a8a","sessionId":"0e254593-63da-5b08-edd4-0783fc8f47be","turnId":"turn-2fbe37e107ed938e2b9446d95c487b5d","inputEntryId":"user-turn-2fbe37e107ed938e2b9446d95c487b5d-1","createdAt":1794276890470,"updatedAt":1794276890483,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.write_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.write_file","display":{"summary":"Writing ANSWER.md","content":"# Root Cause and Fix\n\n## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`). When a second story is published, the `related()` function computes similarity scores against existing stories and stores them in the `similar` list as floats. DynamoDB (via boto3) rejects float values with:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish succeeds because there are no existing stories, so `related()` returns an empty list `[]` with no scores. The second publish fails because it tries to store a float score for the first story.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` import\n2. Modified `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a raw float\n\nThis ensures the score stored in DynamoDB is a Decimal type, which is the only numeric type DynamoDB accepts for non-integer values.\n\n## Changed File\n\n- `src/app.py`: Added Decimal import and converted similarity return value to Decimal\n","suffix":"","verb":"Creating","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Created","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Writing file"},"kind":"file_write","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","content":"# Root Cause and Fix\n\n## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`). When a second story is published, the `related()` function computes similarity scores against existing stories and stores them in the `similar` list as floats. DynamoDB (via boto3) rejects float values with:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish succeeds because there are no existing stories, so `related()` returns an empty list `[]` with no scores. The second publish fails because it tries to store a float score for the first story.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` import\n2. Modified `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a raw float\n\nThis ensures the score stored in DynamoDB is a Decimal type, which is the only numeric type DynamoDB accepts for non-integer values.\n\n## Changed File\n\n- `src/app.py`: Added Decimal import and converted similarity return value to Decimal\n"}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","durationMs":0.0,"output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-RJbWKp/ANSWER.md","content":"# Root Cause and Fix\n\n## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`). When a second story is published, the `related()` function computes similarity scores against existing stories and stores them in the `similar` list as floats. DynamoDB (via boto3) rejects float values with:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish succeeds because there are no existing stories, so `related()` returns an empty list `[]` with no scores. The second publish fails because it tries to store a float score for the first story.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` import\n2. Modified `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a raw float\n\nThis ensures the score stored in DynamoDB is a Decimal type, which is the only numeric type DynamoDB accepts for non-integer values.\n\n## Changed File\n\n- `src/app.py`: Added Decimal import and converted similarity return value to Decimal\n","fileExisted":false,"previousContent":null},"decision":"execute","approvalSource":"bypass","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Created","message":"ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"approvalType":"always"}}
